{"styles":[{"sc":"#ff2600","so":1,"w":2,"ol":true,"fc":"#fffb00","fo":0.502}],"cards":["<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#222222;max-width:238px;\"><div style=\"background:#0e7d46;height:6px;border-radius:3px 3px 0 0;\"></div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:7px 0 0;\">COUNTY BOUNDARY</div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:0 0 2px;\">ARIZONA</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-weight:800;padding:2px 0 6px;\">Pinal County</div><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;\"><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Population</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">539,000 (2025 est.)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">County Seat</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">Florence</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Land Area</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">5,366 sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Density</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">100 / sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Household Income</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$80,300</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Home Value</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$349,000</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#333333;padding:8px 0 2px;border-top:1px solid #eef2f1;margin-top:7px;\">Pinal County occupies the corridor between metropolitan Phoenix and Tucson and has been one of the fastest-growing counties in the United States, with roughly 539,000 residents spread across Casa Grande, Maricopa, Apache Junction, San Tan Valley and Florence. Much of that growth is master-planned residential development absorbing commuters priced out of both metros, which makes it the most rooftop-driven market in Arizona outside Maricopa County. Manufacturing has become a second pillar as electric-vehicle and battery plants have located along the Interstate 10 corridor, alongside a long-established irrigated agriculture base. Large blocks of state trust land shape where growth can go, so development concentrates along the I-10 and US-60 corridors.</div><div style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888888;padding-top:6px;\">Source: U.S. Census Bureau · Data verified: August 30, 2026</div></div>"],"feats":[["Pinal",0,[[32.50162,-111.26687],[32.50135,-111.36373],[32.50135,-111.40526],[32.50138,-111.40595],[32.50133,-111.43202],[32.50133,-111.47727],[32.50137,-111.50458],[32.50134,-111.5266],[32.5014,-111.55208],[32.50139,-111.56925],[32.50677,-111.56926],[32.50676,-111.58103],[32.50673,-111.58141],[32.50671,-111.59081],[32.50663,-111.72621],[32.50665,-111.72637],[32.5067,-111.74404],[32.50667,-111.74419],[32.50664,-111.79254],[32.50666,-111.84104],[32.50663,-111.84873],[32.50666,-111.84892],[32.50666,-111.8559],[32.50663,-111.85599],[32.50668,-111.86824],[32.50666,-111.86844],[32.50665,-111.90914],[32.50666,-111.97521],[32.50669,-111.97542],[32.50666,-112.00069],[32.50661,-112.00365],[32.50675,-112.10967],[32.50675,-112.19112],[32.50672,-112.20362],[32.61987,-112.20356],[32.62099,-112.20359],[32.75633,-112.20356],[32.92177,-112.20346],[32.94173,-112.20349],[32.94207,-112.20348],[32.94204,-112.20302],[33.02915,-112.20298],[33.02915,-112.20215],[33.04188,-112.20215],[33.04604,-112.20213],[33.12582,-112.20215],[33.20328,-112.20212],[33.29047,-112.20204],[33.29046,-112.20318],[33.29606,-112.20321],[33.3105,-112.20317],[33.31048,-112.20309],[33.31029,-112.20291],[33.31016,-112.20257],[33.30994,-112.2023],[33.3095,-112.20211],[33.3091,-112.20214],[33.30875,-112.20225],[33.30848,-112.20214],[33.30823,-112.20214],[3